  <body>
    <main>
      <div class="container">
        <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to portfolio</a>

        <h1>Friends Analytics Dashboard</h1>

        <p class="summary">
          Interactive Tableau dashboard analyzing ratings, viewership, and episode-level metrics across all seasons of the TV series Friends.
        </p>

        <p class="tools">Tableau · Data Visualization · Storytelling · Data Cleaning</p>

        <div class="hero-image">
          <img
            src="/projects/friends-tableau-dashboard.jpg"
            alt="Friends Analytics Dashboard"
          />
        </div>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>Project Overview</h2>
          <p>
            This project analyzes multiple datasets related to the TV series <strong>Friends</strong> to explore patterns in episode performance, 
            audience engagement, and character dialogue across the series.
            Several datasets were combined, including episode metadata, character quotes, 
            and relationship information. Initial exploration and light preprocessing 
            were performed in Python, while the majority of data cleaning, modeling, and visualization were completed directly in Tableau.
            The final interactive dashboard examines episode ratings, broadcast viewership, and character dialogue trends 
            across all ten seasons. Special focus was placed on comparing the highest-rated episodes with the 
            most-viewed broadcasts, revealing differences between audience reception and live broadcast popularity.
            Additional analysis of iconic quotes explores dialogue distribution across characters and highlights 
            how memorable phrases are associated with specific characters throughout the series.
          </p>
          
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>What I Worked On</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Performed exploratory data analysis and initial data cleaning across multiple Friends datasets including episode metadata, quotes, and character information.</li>
            <li>Prepared and transformed datasets for analysis, addressing inconsistencies such as naming variations and incomplete values.</li>
            <li>Built the primary Tableau dashboard layout and visual design, incorporating the recognizable Friends typography and visual style.</li>
            <li>Designed and implemented visualizations analyzing episode ratings, viewership trends, and season-level performance.</li>
            <li>Created analyses of the top 10 highest-rated episodes and the top 10 most-viewed episodes, highlighting overlaps and differences between audience ratings and broadcast popularity.</li>
            <li>Developed quote analysis visuals showing character dialogue distribution and frequency of well-known phrases across the series.</li>
            <li>Curated and cleaned tooltip content to present relevant contextual information without overwhelming the viewer.</li>
            <li>Configured dashboard interactions, filters, and axis formatting to improve clarity and usability of the visualizations.</li>
            <li>Collaborated on defining key metrics and KPIs used throughout the dashboard.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>Key Highlights</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Interactive Tableau dashboard analyzing episode ratings, audience viewership, and dialogue patterns across all ten seasons of Friends.</li>
            <li>Comparison of highest-rated episodes versus highest-viewed episodes, revealing differences between critical reception and broadcast popularity.</li>
            <li>Dialogue analysis of iconic quotes across characters to explore dialogue distribution and cultural impact.</li>
            <li>Dashboard design inspired by the visual identity of the Friends series while maintaining analytical clarity.</li>
            <li>Integration of multiple datasets including episodes, quotes, and character information to create enriched analytical views.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

